Final practical recommendations & tradeoffs
    • For short torque pulses, relatively modest bus caps (tens of mF at low voltage) are usually sufficient. Use polymer electrolytic + film/MLCC HF decoupling for best ESR/ESL performance.
    • For significant regenerative absorption, do not rely solely on DC caps — use battery absorption + brake resistor + active regen control, or add a dedicated supercap bank sized expressly for regen (but that becomes heavy/expensive).
    • Use RCD clamps or carefully tuned RC snubbers to protect MOSFETs from switching spikes — cheaper and more robust than relying on TVS alone.
    • Add pre-charge and inrush protection to prevent cap stress and contactor damage.
    • Always check cap ripple current rating and temperature derating; mount caps with adequate cooling.
